# Swaps: Baseline v0, piece by piece

There is no dataset [P15], so no row cites a D tag. The "regime" here is the threat model [P3], the ERC-7562 validation rules [E2], a 1-week build by 2-4 strong Solidity devs [P16], and assumed generalist plus protocol-literate judges [A1]. X1 (the attack-suite results table) and X4/X5 are defined in EXPERIMENTS.md and run during the build.

Phase C re-run 2 (CR18-CR31, 2026-10-24) changed these rows: Recipient risk (now a swap: D3), the new rows Payee decision rule, Payee uncertainty, Score attestation, Trust scoring service, Outcome signal and Simulator check, plus Testing, Data / eval set, UI and Deployment. It also corrects the Policy expression row: per-argument rules are not Zodiac-only [E50][E51].

| Piece | Baseline | Best alternative [E#] | Swap? | Why in this regime |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Data / eval set | none; ad hoc tests | Attack suite modelled on AgentDojo/WASP end-to-end attacker-goal scoring, with every attack mapped to an on-chain outcome [E27][E28][E29] | **Swap** (build our own): X1 becomes a results table, 4 wallet configs x about 10 cards x 2 metrics (funds lost; legit new-payee payments blocked) [X1] | No dataset [P15][A4]. Benchmarks mock their finance tools, so "attack success" there is not "funds lost". The second metric prices openness, which is TRACE's fraud-openness trade-off [E34]. |
| Account | SimpleAccount fork | ERC-7579 modular account (Kernel, Nexus) + session validator [E3][E6][E7] | **Keep** SimpleAccount-style account; write the policy as one separate `AgentPolicy` contract with a 7579-shaped interface (install on Nexus = stretch, first in the cut order) | Owning the account lets us close the ERC-1271 path and the self-call/upgrade path (T2, T12) in code we control. Full 7579 or 7702 shaping adds days no generalist judge sees [A1]. |
| EntryPoint | unspecified | v0.8: userOpHash becomes an EIP-712 typed hash [E5] | **Swap**: pin v0.8 only | One pinned version removes the v0.7/v0.8 hash ambiguity. Typed hashes make owner prompts readable (R11). Bundler support on Base Sepolia is assumption A9. |
| Signature check | ecrecover over userOpHash | OZ ECDSA with malleability checks; EntryPoint 2D nonce with one key per session [E1] | **Keep** | Standard and correct. The work is in tests (wrong chain, wrong EntryPoint, replayed nonce). |
| Policy expression | target+selector allowlist; decoded amount for transfer/approve | Per-parameter conditions: Zodiac Roles [E16], Kernel call policy [E50], Smart Sessions UniActionPolicy ParamRule [E51]; composable caveats [E13] | **Partial swap**: one declarative struct with static-word argument rules (`EQ_SELF`, `IN_RECIPIENTS`, `LTE`, `EQ`); asset-moving selectors (`transfer`, `transferFrom`, `approve`, `setApprovalForAll`, NFT `safeTransferFrom`) are refused unless an argument rule binds `to`/`spender`/`operator` [E56][E57] | A target-only allowlist misses the ERC-20 `to` (T4). Argument rules exist in several engines, so they are table stakes, not novelty. A general condition language is too much to build and test in a week. |
| Spend metering | decoded amount argument | Measure the balance and allowance delta of tracked assets around the call, in execution | **Swap** (D2) | Decoding covers only functions we know. An allowed merchant's `buy()` or a router can move tokens we never decode; a delta counts what actually left. |
| Daily limit | counter in execution | Rolling window or token bucket in execution; periodic buckets reset [E14][E17]; TIMESTAMP is banned in validation [E2] | **Swap**: per-key and account-wide token buckets, checked in execution | A calendar bucket allows 2x at the boundary (T7). Execution is the only phase that may read time [E2]. |
| Per-tx limit | decoded amount <= cap in validation | measured delta <= cap in execution, plus the decoded amount as an early reject in validation | **Swap** (pairs with metering) | The early reject keeps bundlers from carrying ops sure to fail; the delta is the real bound. |
| Expiry | `validUntil` in validationData | same [E1][E2] | **Keep** | Already right, and ERC-7562 forces it [E2]. |
| Gas | not handled | Cap `maxFeePerGas`, gas limits and `paymasterAndData` per session key in validation; gas credit debited in validation from account storage | **Swap** (small) | With no paymaster, a leaked key burns the prefund through fees (T5). Budget checks that revert in execution still pay gas, and an attacker-run bundler collects it, so the per-key gas caps and credit bound that griefing (CR19, CR25). |
| Off-UserOp signatures (ERC-1271) | not considered | Smart Sessions ERC-1271 policies [E7]; Kernel signature policy [E6] | **New piece** (D1): `isValidSignature` refuses the agent key by default; opt-in x402 voucher envelope only if X3 passes | x402 "exact" = EIP-3009 `transferWithAuthorization` [E20]; USDC [E21] and Permit2 [E22] accept contract signatures, so an agent key that 1271 accepts spends with no UserOp. |
| Out-of-policy approval | owner signs the UserOp | Owner signs EIP-712 `OutcomeApproval` (chainId, account, nonce, target, selector, payee, maxOutflow, callDataHash, validUntil); single use by nonce | **Swap** | Misleading signing requests drove most 2025 signature phishing losses [E26]; an injected agent writes the request text, so that text is untrusted (T11). |
| Revocation | none | one owner tx flips `revoked`; validation checks it; owner can bump the attestation epoch | **Keep** (simple flag) | R14 needs it; nothing more complex helps. |
| Recipient risk | static allowlist | TRACE two-track recipient policy (D3): signed tiers; proven payees get normal caps, unproven or unattested payees share a small account-wide exploration budget, flagged payees go to owner approval or block [E34] | **Swap** (CR18; about 30% of the effort, one slide) | In an open agent market payees are pseudonymous and new ones appear daily, so a static list either blocks every legit newcomer or gets loosened by hand. TRACE shows pure greedy selection serves 66/700 honest providers vs 125/700 with exploration [E34], that a single-buyer (partitioned) view makes greedy unsafe (32.0 vs 6.4 sats strat fraud) [E34], and that fraud defense and newcomer discovery need separate tracks with independent budgets [E34]. On-chain, the exploration track turns that into a hard bound: loss to new payees <= explorationCap per window, even with an injected agent [A19]. |
| Payee decision rule | allowlisted or not | tier from attestation: proven / unproven / flagged; missing or expired attestation = unproven, never proven | **New** | Gated hierarchy that cannot contradict itself: the only upgrade path is a valid attestor signature, and every failure mode (no attestation, expired, wrong chain, wrong wallet, rotated attestor) lands in the bounded track by construction. |
| Payee uncertainty | none | TRACE Bayesian 95% LCB with a Beta(1,3) prior; cold-start payees sit near the prior [E34] | **New** (from the user's paper) | An unknown payee is not guessed good or bad. It is sent to the bounded exploration track, which plays the role of abstention. |
| Score attestation | none | EIP-712 `ScoreAttestation{recipient, tier, validUntil, epoch}` with domain {name, version, chainId, verifyingContract = wallet} [{EIP712}], carried in `userOp.signature`, ecrecovered against an owner-set attestor; validUntil folded into validationData like the reference VerifyingPaymaster [{VPM}] | **New piece** (established pattern, not novelty) | Validation may read only the account's own storage and no TIMESTAMP [E2], so a shared on-chain score registry is out. The typed domain blocks cross-chain and cross-wallet replay. |
| Trust scoring service | none | port TRACE scoring from the public Trace_CIKM code [E58] (LCB, smoothed default risk + CUSUM, PPR from an honest seed, counterparty entropy, edge-to-job Sybil ratio, clique and contamination penalties [E34]) into an HTTP/JSON attestor | **New** (backend service) | The code is TypeScript and Prisma-coupled, and the public tree is not runnable as published [E58][A21], so the port reuses the scoring modules behind a small store. A raw on-chain reputation feed is not used as the score, because ERC-8004 reviews show coordinated Sybil funding [{XIONG}]. |
| Outcome signal | none | x402 settlement receipt + delivery check [{X402RESP}]; owner- or verifier-signed outcome (the D2 signed outcome); ERC-8004 feedback only as a discounted input [{ERC8004}][{XIONG}] | **New** | TRACE needs a binary success/default per job [E34]. An injected agent would report whatever helps the attacker, so agent-only outcomes are ignored [A22]. |
| Agent | scripted bot | open-weight LLM agent (pick the backbone from b3 [E30]) plus the scripted bot for the suite | **Swap** for the demo; keep the bot for tests | "Any open model" [P10][A3]. Model-level defenses fail [E39], so the agent stays untrusted. |
| Agent-side defense | none | CaMeL [E24], injection detectors [E23] | **Keep none** (by design) | Adaptive attacks beat 12 defenses at >90% ASR [E39]. The wallet must hold with a fully hijacked agent [P3]. |
| Off-chain policy engine | none | CDP [E18], Privy [E19], presidio-x402 [E38] | **Keep none** | They are bypassed by a key or host leak. The attestor only labels payees; the caps live on-chain and a compromised attestor stays inside globalCap. |
| Testing | Foundry unit tests | Foundry invariant tests with handlers [{FOUNDRY}]; Halmos symbolic tests [{HALMOS}]; DeFiHackLabs-style replays [E31]; bundler-spec-tests [E32] | **Swap**: invariants I1-I9, fuzzed calldata, Halmos on the bounded policy-check function, THREAT_MODEL.md mapping attack -> defense -> test name [X5] | Security correctness is what protocol-literate judges probe [A1]. Halmos is second in the cut order; fuzzing stays. |
| Simulator check (analysis) | none | fork the Trace_CIKM simulator [E58], add TRACE + exploration budget B, sweep B against the paper's policies [E34] | **New** (X4, pre-registered) | Tells us whether the exploration track moves the fraud vs served-honest frontier, or only gives the hard bound. No claim before the runs [X4]. |
| UI | approval web page | owner dashboard, approval inbox, phone approval | **Cut from this build** (CR29) | Backend only: owner approval is exercised with a scripted signer and typedData test vectors [A18]; the UI comes later and calls the same APIs. |
| Deployment | Base Sepolia | Base mainnet (user already runs x402 there [A2][A5]) | **Keep** testnet; mainnet only for X3's one receipt, and a mainnet bounty only after X1 and X5 pass and the event rules allow it (CR27) | The demo needs explorer links, not real money. |
